      "dom_id": "question-164549",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Identify the surface ${y}^{2}-{z}^{2}-x-4y-6z-4=0.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we complete the square in the $y$ and $z$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}-x-4y-6z-4 & =0 \\\\ ({y}^{2}-4y)-({z}^{2}+6z)-x-4 & =0 \\\\ (y-2)^{2}-4-(z+3)^{2}+9-x-4 & =0 \\\\ (y-2)^{2}-(z+3)^{2}+1-x & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, by rearranging, we get the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2}-(z+3)^{2}+1-x & =0 \\\\ (y-2)^{2}-(z+3)^{2} & =x-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of a hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $(1,2,-3).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [],
      "answer_fields_complete": null,
      "result": "Correct",
      "proof_feedback": null,
